# Supply Chain Audit Rule

Use this rule only when intentionally auditing security risk. Prefer global User Rules for recurring use; add this Project Rule only when the team wants it versioned.

Default mode is audit-only:

- Read files and logs.
- Do not create reports or helper files in the project by default.
- Do not edit code, workflows, lockfiles or configs unless explicitly requested.
- Do not run `npm install`, `pnpm install`, `yarn install`, `composer install`, builds, migrations or deploys before triage.
- Do not download dumps, leaked personal data or criminal-forum material.
- Classify evidence before saying compromise or breach is confirmed.

Findings must include severity, evidence, impact, IOC, MITRE ATT&CK when applicable, exploitability and correction.
